2026-09-03T17:03Z Minh Ha-Duong ruled REFRAME (DECISIONS.md): one adversarial library plus a derived question bank, replacing the 25-bullet checklist as the operational shape (the checklist stays as a coverage ledger). Question count derived from a per-dimension sub-case tally, ≈97, landing near the author's own "about 100" instinct as corroboration rather than proof. Reuse across documents bounded at 4 per question, per the author's follow-up, to stop the tally being satisfied by loading a handful of flexible documents. Tracker structure added; the harness triplet is the first child to file, unblocked by the 9 browser-only sourcing fetches.
2026-09-03T18:20Z Minh Ha-Duong ruled REVISED TALLY: exactly 200 questions (up from ≈97), each dimension row restated as what it tests plus a worked example rather than a bare label, and the reuse bound moved to a floor of at least 5 questions per document, no ceiling, replacing PR #315's ceiling of at most 4 documents per question. That floor reverses PR #315's anti-gaming rationale on purpose: with 200 questions and a >=5-reuse floor the fixture needs at most ~40 distinct documents (200/5) under the common-case assumption of one document per question, concentrating cost in question-authoring against already-sourced hard cases rather than in further sourcing. The growth to 200 crosses two axes the author named concretely (structural marks, extraction-cap boundaries) against the 3 MUST-tier languages (EN/FR/VI) already committed for sourcing, not the full 9-language roster -- SHOULD-tier documents carrying tables/footnotes/captions specifically would be a materially larger sourcing lift than this ticket's SHOULD-language row already commits to, per this ticket's own sourcing-difficulty log. Both the count and the reuse floor stay first-pass/adjustable, same standing as the ≈97 table they replace
